ics2txt.py:
prints the events of an ics file as text.

ldjson2ics.py:
extracts schema.org ld+json reservations (hotel, flight, train, ...)
from an email and converts them to ics.

ics2caldav.py:
uploads the events of an ics file to a CalDAV calendar.
Give server (or calendar) URL, user and calendar name (-u/-U/-c or CALDAV_URL,
CALDAV_USER, CALDAV_CALENDAR in ~/.config/ics2caldav) and it discovers the
collection URL; -l lists the calendars. Password from CALDAV_PASSCMD,
~/.netrc or prompt.

mutt macro to add a reservation mail to the calendar:
macro index,pager \ec "<pipe-message>ldjson2ics | ics2caldav<enter>" "add reservation to calendar"
